    "result_text": "Done. I agreed with the finding and applied it.\n\n## What changed\n- **`OwnerAddress.compose(String line1, String line2)`** \u2014 new method that owns the composition rule (normalize both lines, append `line2` after a single space when non-blank, return just `line1` otherwise). This is the \"stored/returned/compared form\" the class already claims to define.\n- **`OwnerAddress` javadoc** \u2014 updated to state the class now also owns the structured-address composition rule, and the \"single definition to agree on\" line now covers both the flat and composed cases rather than only the flat field.\n- **`ValidateOwnerFields.service`** \u2014 the inline `line1 + \" \" + line2` ternary is gone; it now calls `OwnerAddress.compose(...)` and stays focused on presence/blank validation and write-back.\n\nNormalisation is idempotent, so passing the already-normalised lines into `compose` (which normalises again) yields the identical result \u2014 no behaviour change, and the composition rule lives in exactly one place.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, **BUILD SUCCESS**. (The `mvn verify` JaCoCo coverage gate remains unsatisfiable with the 2-test sample suite, as before and unrelated to this refactor.)",
