        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change works end-to-end, but it splits what was a deliberately centralized rule.\n\n**Finding \u2014 address composition belongs in `OwnerAddress`, not inline in the validator**\n\n`OwnerAddress` is documented as the \"Single source of truth for the owner address normalisation rule\" and describes `normalize` as returning \"The stored/returned/compared form.\" After this change, that promise is only half true: `normalize` still produces each field's canonical token form, but the *actual* stored/returned/compared value is now the **composed** string (`line1 + \" \" + line2`), and that composition rule lives inline in `ValidateOwnerFields.service` (lines 52\u201354) rather than in `OwnerAddress`. The single source of truth is now spread across two classes.\n\nConcretely:\n- Add a method to `OwnerAddress` that owns the composition rule, e.g. `static String compose(String line1, String line2)` (normalize both, append line2 after a single space when non-blank, return the canonical composed form). This is exactly the \"stored/returned/compared form\" the class already claims to define, and the spec states it as an address rule (\"a composed 'address' string equal to the normalized addressLine1, with a single space and the normalized addressLine2 appended when addressLine2 is present\").\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` then calls that single method and stays focused on its one job \u2014 presence/blank validation and write-back \u2014 instead of also carrying the ternary string-building for the canonical value.\n- Update the `OwnerAddress` class javadoc, which still says normalisation has \"one consumer\" and only describes the flat-field case; it no longer reflects the structured/compose responsibility.\n\nThis keeps the method from accreting address-shaping logic and restores the \"one definition to agree on\" intent the helper class was created for. The model, entity getters/setters, schema columns, and OpenAPI additions are all idiomatic and well-placed \u2014 the only structural issue is the misplaced composition logic."
